 finding the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure and looking into the orchestrator error.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01Pinjrin5D4bFS7oFLDsUVr", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_019M4ydrqEXSBXPWiycLHSnu", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01EdNuV5kfibfsq4sq1ZwFjT", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01EEL3sgSL1nrMwdShWv56Nb", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The rollback only reached us-east. Rolling back to the same target version is safe to repeat, so I'll retry once.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_016RJtCRSWVkk1EiEggcMrbc", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_0146o8Si8AjZh6N3yYTsbGpH", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01BQFpzysWHGzd48pLz1XRDE", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01SNqn9sRmFMseNroSbzuE7F", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "checkout-api v2.3.1 failing health checks \u2013 rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "After deploying v2.3.1, checkout-api failed health checks in all regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west) with an error rate of about 18%. v2.3.1-rc was also unhealthy. Rolled back to v2.3.0, the most recent healthy release. The first rollback attempt stopped after us-east because of an orchestrator error, which left the service on mixed versions. A retry completed the rollback in all regions. Current state: v2.3.0 in us-east, us-west and eu-west, healthy, error rate 0.2%. Follow-ups: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure and look into the orchestrator error that stopped the first rollback.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-v2.3.1-rollback-sev2"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01WUdWH6nP5w1zXta6GU3ifF", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "checkout-api is rolled back to v2.3.0 in all regions and is healthy again, and SEV2 incident INC-0001 is open.\n\n- **Rollback:** v2.3.0 is the most recent healthy release. v2.3.1 and its release candidate (v2.3.1-rc) both failed health checks. The first rollback attempt stopped after us-east because of an orchestrator error, so the regions were briefly on different versions. A second attempt finished the rollback.\n- **Current state:** us-east, us-west and eu-west are all on v2.3.0. The service reports healthy, and the error rate is down from 18% to 0.2%.\n- **Incident:** The request to open the incident timed out, but the incident list shows it was created, so I didn't send it again to avoid paging on-call twice. INC-0001 describes the failure, the rollback (including the stopped first attempt) and two follow-ups: finding the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure and looking into the orchestrator error.", "type": "text"}]}]}